# Day 31/50 — Data Structures

A computer doesn't just need information
It also needs a way to organize it.

That's where **Data Structures** come in.

Arrays, Linked Lists, Stacks, Queues, Trees and Graphs — each structure stores and organizes data differently.

An array keeps elements in an indexed sequence. 
A stack follows LIFO.
A queue follows FIFO. 
Trees represent hierarchical relationships, while
Graphs connect different nodes.

The choice of structure can change how efficiently a problem is solved.

It's interesting how the same information can become easier or harder to work with depending on how it's arranged.

**Because sometimes, the way we organize information matters just as much as the information itself**
